# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Internal architecture notes (see concepts/README.md), anchored to the repository root. ROADMAP.md
# carries every open work item.
#
# The third-party corpus — the OpenADR 3 specification mirror (Apache-2.0, © OpenADR Alliance) —
# lives at `concepts/reference/openadr3-specification/` and is covered by this line: fetched by
# `cargo xtask spec-sync` (or into `$OPENADR_REFERENCE`), not vendored.
CONCEPT.md
/concepts/

# This project's own feature specifications, and the Spec Kit machinery that produces them: one
# `specs/NNN-slug/` per ROADMAP item, `.specify/memory/constitution.md`, the threatspec extension and
# the `/speckit-*` skills. Same rule as `concepts/` — internal. Until 2026-11-21 `specs/` held the
# specification mirror now under `concepts/reference/`; a stale copy is ignored by the same line.
# Matching eebus, sepa and ocpp-kit.
/specs/
/.specify/
/.claude/

# Zola build output
site/public/

# `examples/ven` persists which reports it has filed, so a restart does not refile them. That is a
# run's state, not the repository's.
ven-state.json

.DS_Store
# `openadr dev` writes its per-run credentials here; never commit them.
.openadr-dev.env
